% Probe: horizontal spacing at every CJK/Latin script boundary, and the
% unconditional half-width kern `ideographic_single` (upstream
% `convertText.ml:267-283`) attaches to fullwidth punctuation.
%
% Each paragraph is ONE boundary shape, short enough to stay on one line so
% `pdftotext` reports the words in a predictable order. Read the numbers as
% ADVANCES within a single engine (xMin of the latin word minus xMin of the
% CJK run before it): the CJK face is the same file in both engines, so that
% quantity is comparable across them, while an absolute latin xMin is not.
%
%   A  ideograph  -> latin        (no punctuation anywhere)
%   B  kuten `。` -> latin        (JLFS, trailing hwkern upstream)
%   C  touten `、` -> latin       (JLCM, trailing hwkern upstream)
%   D  close `）` -> latin        (JLCP, trailing hwkern upstream)
%   E  latin -> open `（`         (JLOP, LEADING hwkern upstream)
%   F  latin -> close `）`        (suppressed: is_close_punctuation lbc2)
%   G  open `（` -> latin         (suppressed: is_open_punctuation lbc1)
%   H  latin -> ideograph         (plain, no punctuation)
%   I  nakaten `・` -> latin      (JLMD, quarter kern both sides)
@require: stdjabook

document (|
  title = {interscript probe};
  author = {};
  show-title = false;
  show-toc = false;
|) '<
  +p{漢字 alpha 漢字}
  +p{漢字。 bravo 漢字}
  +p{漢字、 charlie 漢字}
  +p{漢字） delta 漢字}
  +p{echo （漢字}
  +p{foxtrot ）漢字}
  +p{漢字（ golf 漢字}
  +p{hotel 漢字}
  +p{漢字・ india 漢字}
>
